Hi,

With the last version of Tinn-R, I have a new problem that is weird: sometimes when I ask it to close (by clicking the window's X button) it starts an infinite loop of activating & deactivating the window, but does not close. Even worse, after 1 minute or so, Windows feels bad about this and I hear the PC speaker beeping... like if the PC was asking for help. Then I have to shut down Windows, and then accept to "force" the application to close (as proposed by Windows).

Unfortunately, I do not know how to reproduce the issue... but if you have some idea on the causes of that issue?... I would like it very much to be solved... because it feels bad to have an IDE that fails to close and forces me to close the PC.

Thanks, and have a nice day.

Best,

Marc

